<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polynesia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Polynesia is the region of the central and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> within a triangle formed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Rapa Nui</a> (Easter Island), with over a thousand islands. Its peoples descend from seafarers of the Lapita culture who reached Tonga and Samoa nearly 3,000 years ago, then spread across the eastern Pacific in long canoe voyages between about 1000 and 1300 CE, sharing related languages, chiefly ranks and marae temples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polynesia.jpg" alt="Polynesia" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hobe / Holger Behr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_OC-Polynesia.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
